  "function": {
    "uniprot_function": "Serine/threonine-protein kinase involved in transcription regulation, p53/TP53-mediated cellular apoptosis and regulation of the cell cycle. Acts as a corepressor of several transcription factors, including SMAD1 and POU4F1/Brn3a and probably NK homeodomain transcription factors. Phosphorylates p53/TP53, CREB1, DAXX, DAZAP2, EP300, CBX4, CTNNB1, CTBP1, HMGA1, PML, and RUNX1. Plays a key role in responding to DNA damage by regulating p53/TP53 phosphorylation at 'Ser-46' in response to severe DNA damage, promoting apoptosis. Also involved in transcriptional activation of TP53 through promoter-specific phosphorylation of CREB1. Can phosphorylate beta-catenin (CTNNB1) at 'Ser-33' and 'Ser-37', targeting it for proteasomal degradation independent of GSK3B, acting as a negative regulator of Wnt signaling. Phosphorylates DAXX, which is essential for DAXX interaction with HIPK2 and subsequent apoptosis. Its ability to phosphorylate transcription factors appears to require its association with PML nuclear bodies.",
    "catalytic_activity": "ATP + L-seryl-[protein] = ADP + H(+) + O-phospho-L-seryl-[protein]; ATP + L-threonyl-[protein] = ADP + H(+) + O-phospho-L-threonyl-[protein]",
    "subcellular_location": ["Nucleus", "Nuclear body", "PML body", "Cytoplasm"],
    "tissue_specificity": "Tissue enriched in brain with ubiquitous nuclear expression. Tau specificity score: 0.54. Cell type enhanced in somatotrophs and plasma cells. Expression cluster: oligodendrocytes-myelination.",
