    "pathway_role_summary": "HIPK2 is a central kinase in DNA damage response pathways, phosphorylating p53 at Ser46 to promote apoptosis. Acts as negative regulator of Wnt signaling by phosphorylating beta-catenin. Regulates TGF-beta signaling through DAXX and JNK activation. Functions as tumor suppressor through multiple mechanisms including CtBP degradation and transcriptional corepression. Critical regulator of PML nuclear body function and cellular senescence."
