    "data_quality_notes": "Complete amino acid sequence not directly accessible via web scraping; available at UniProt Q9H2X6. Some kinetic parameters (Kd, Km, kcat) not available in literature for most interactions. Disease mutation data limited to reported cases in literature. Most interaction data is qualitative; quantitative binding affinities are sparse. Isoform sequences require direct UniProt access.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "HIPK2 is critical for Wnt pathway regulation through direct beta-catenin phosphorylation at Ser33/Ser37, independent of destruction complex. Acts as DNA damage sensor phosphorylating p53 at Ser46 for apoptosis. Multiple E3 ligases (Siah-1, FBXO3, WSB1) provide tight basal regulation with DNA damage-responsive stabilization. PML nuclear body localization essential for function. Three isoforms with distinct functions (full-length, Δe8 stable variant, short cytokinesis-specific). Rich post-translational modification crosstalk (phosphorylation, ubiquitination, sumoylation, acetylation) creates complex regulatory network suitable for rule-based modeling."
